{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n, _memo={1: 1, 2: 1}):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    The sequence is defined by P(1)=1, P(2)=1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Calculate P(n-1) which is needed for both recursive terms\n    p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1, _memo)\n\n    # Apply the recursive formula\n    result = sequence(p_n_minus_1, _memo) + sequence(n - p_n_minus_1, _memo)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
