{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(s: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string\n    the given number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _perform_left_rotation(binary_string: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Performs a single left rotation on the given binary string.\"\"\"\n        if not binary_string:\n            return \"\"\n        return binary_string[1:] + binary_string[0]\n\n    def _binary_to_decimal(binary_string: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts a binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n        return int(binary_string, 2)\n\n    def _is_odd(decimal_number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a decimal integer is odd.\"\"\"\n        return decimal_number % 2 != 0\n\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_s = s\n\n    for _ in range(n):\n        current_s = _perform_left_rotation(current_s)\n        decimal_val = _binary_to_decimal(current_s)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_val):\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_list: list[list]) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements in a given nested list.\n\n    Args:\n        nested_list: A list of lists, where each inner list contains comparable elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        A set containing elements that are present in all sublists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_list:\n        return set()\n\n    common_elements = set(nested_list[0])\n\n    for sublist in nested_list[1:]:\n        common_elements.intersection_update(set(sublist))\n        if not common_elements: # Optimization: if no common elements left, break early.\n            break\n\n    return common_elements"}
