{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "def find_solution(a, b, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integers x and y that satisfy ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) or None if no solution exists.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _gcd(num1, num2):\n        # Returns the absolute value of the greatest common divisor.\n        num1, num2 = abs(num1), abs(num2)\n        while num2:\n            num1, num2 = num2, num1 % num2\n        return num1\n\n    def _extended_gcd(num1, num2):\n        # Implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm: finds g, x, y such that num1*x + num2*y = g.\n        if num2 == 0:\n            return (num1, 1, 0)\n        else:\n            g, x, y = _extended_gcd(num2, num1 % num2)\n            return (g, y, x - (num1 // num2) * y)\n\n    # Handle the trivial case where both a and b are zero\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n\n    # Calculate g = gcd(a, b)\n    g = _gcd(a, b)\n\n    # If n is not divisible by g, no integer solution exists\n    if n % g != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find x0, y0 for a*x0 + b*y0 = g_val\n    g_val, x0, y0 = _extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # Ensure g_val is positive (matching canonical GCD) and adjust x0, y0 accordingly\n    if g_val < 0:\n        g_val = -g_val\n        x0 = -x0\n        y0 = -y0\n\n    # Scale x0, y0 to find a particular solution (x_p, y_p) for a*x + b*y = n\n    factor = n // g_val\n    x_p = x0 * factor\n    y_p = y0 * factor\n\n    # Normalize (x_p, y_p) to get the solution with the smallest non-negative x\n    # This ensures consistency for assert statements or specific solution requirements.\n    if b != 0:\n        # Calculate the period for x: abs(b)/g\n        x_period = abs(b) // g\n\n        # Calculate the smallest non-negative x\n        x_final = x_p % x_period\n        if x_final < 0:\n            x_final += x_period\n\n        # Calculate k, the number of periods x_p was away from x_final\n        k = (x_final - x_p) // (b // g) # k can be negative\n\n        # Adjust y_p based on k\n        y_final = y_p + k * (a // g)\n        return (x_final, y_final)\n    else: # If b is 0, a is not 0 (handled by above if a=0,b=0). Solution is (n/a, 0).\n        return (x_p, y_p) # which will be (n//a, 0)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/162", "solution": "def sum_series(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the series (n - 2*i) from i=0 to n // 2 (inclusive).\n    The series stops adding terms if a term becomes less than or equal to 0,\n    following the pattern n + (n-2) + (n-4)... (until n-x <= 0).\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate from i=0 to n // 2, inclusive.\n    for i in range(n // 2 + 1):\n        term = n - 2 * i\n        # Stop adding terms if a term is non-positive after the initial term.\n        if term <= 0 and i > 0:\n            break\n        total_sum += term\n    return total_sum"}
