{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total count of prime numbers strictly less than the given input number.\n    It orchestrates the prime counting process using a helper function to check primality.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a given integer is a prime number.\n        This helper function efficiently checks for primality.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        \n        # Check for divisors from 3 up to the square root of num, only checking odd numbers\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    if limit <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Iterate through numbers from 2 up to limit - 1\n    for num in range(2, limit):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            prime_count += 1\n            \n    return prime_count"}
