{"task_id": "Mbpp/273", "solution": "def substract_elements(tuple1: tuple[int | float, ...], tuple2: tuple[int | float, ...]) -> tuple[int | float, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Subtracts elements of the second tuple from the first tuple element-wise.\n\n    Raises ValueError if input tuples have different lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of elements.\")\n\n    result_elements = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        result_elements.append(tuple1[i] - tuple2[i])\n    return tuple(result_elements)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/274", "solution": "import math\ndef _binomial_coefficient(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(n, k).\"\"\"\n    return math.factorial(n) // (math.factorial(k) * math.factorial(n - k))\ndef even_binomial_Coeff_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of even index binomial coefficients for a positive integer n.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(0, n + 1, 2):\n        total_sum += _binomial_coefficient(n, k)\n    return total_sum"}
