{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "def sub_list(list1: list[int], list2: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise subtraction of two input lists.\n    Raises ValueError if the input lists have different lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must have the same length for element-wise subtraction.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        result.append(list1[i] - list2[i])\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "import collections\ndef validate(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer 'num'\n    is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        num = abs(num)\n\n    if num == 0:\n        return False\n\n    num_str = str(num)\n    digit_frequencies = collections.Counter(int(d) for d in num_str)\n\n    for digit, frequency in digit_frequencies.items():\n        if frequency > digit:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
