{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of possible unordered pairs from a list where both elements are unequal.\n    This function orchestrates the generation and checking of pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _generate_unordered_pairs(input_list: list[int]) -> set[frozenset[int]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Generates all unique unordered pairs from elements at distinct indices within the input list.\n        \"\"\"\n        unique_pairs = set()\n        n = len(input_list)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                pair = frozenset({input_list[i], input_list[j]})\n                unique_pairs.add(pair)\n        return unique_pairs\n\n    def _is_unequal_pair(pair: frozenset[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if the two elements within a given frozenset pair are unequal.\n        \"\"\"\n        return len(pair) == 2\n\n    unequal_count = 0\n    all_unique_pairs = _generate_unordered_pairs(input_list)\n\n    for pair in all_unique_pairs:\n        if _is_unequal_pair(pair):\n            unequal_count += 1\n\n    return unequal_count"}
