{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "def multiply_elements(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of adjacent elements in a tuple.\n\n    Args:\n        input_tuple: A tuple of numbers (integers or floats).\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple where the i-th element is the product of the i-th and (i+1)-th\n        elements of the input tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_tuple) < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        result.append(input_tuple[i] * input_tuple[i+1])\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/728", "solution": "def sum_list(list1: list[int], list2: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the element-wise sum of two input lists of integers.\n    Raises ValueError if lists have different lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Lists must have the same length\")\n\n    result = []\n    for a, b in zip(list1, list2):\n        result.append(a + b)\n    return result"}
