{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, number_of_items: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Handles empty lists and rotation counts greater than list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate effective rotation count (BR5)\n    # Ensure number_of_items is non-negative, though modulo handles it effectively for positive inputs\n    # If number_of_items could be negative, we might do `abs(number_of_items) % n` or raise an error.\n    # Given the context 'non-negative integer' we assume it's already >= 0.\n    effective_rotation = number_of_items % n\n\n    # Slice the list into two parts and concatenate for right rotation\n    # The last 'effective_rotation' elements move to the front\n    return input_list[n - effective_rotation:] + input_list[:n - effective_rotation]"}
