{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, element: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using a modified binary search.\n    It returns the 0-based index of the last occurrence, or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find further right for the last occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
